Package: coinbase-mcp-server
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 nodejs (>= 24),
Description: MCP server for the Coinbase Advanced Trade API
 coinbase-mcp-server is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets
 AI assistants interact with the Coinbase Advanced Trade API: account
 balances, order placement, portfolio and product data, 24 technical
 indicators, chart-pattern and sentiment analysis, and market-event
 tools, alongside an included autonomous trading Skill.
 .
 WARNING: when configured with live API keys this software can place
 real trades and move real funds on your Coinbase account. Use
 read-only or sandbox keys during evaluation and dry-run mode before
 trading with real money.
 .
 The server runs over stdio (--stdio, for desktop MCP hosts such as
 Claude Code) or HTTP (default, port 3000 unless overridden by PORT).
 Credentials are supplied via the COINBASE_API_KEY_NAME and
 COINBASE_PRIVATE_KEY environment variables.

Package: mcprack-mcp-server-coinbase
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 mcprack (>= 1.5.1),
 coinbase-mcp-server (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: Registers Coinbase MCP server into mcprack catalog
 Companion package for coinbase-mcp-server. Installing it registers the
 coinbase-mcp-server binary (stdio mode) as an available MCP server in
 the local mcprack instance; removing it unregisters it again.
